WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.440
House of the Dragon is a Game&nbsp;
of Thrones prequel show that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.440
confirmed by HBO’s president to air in 2022. 
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:27.280
showrunners and executive producers. George R.&nbsp;
R. Martin will also serve as executive producer.
&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.800
It is based on George RR Martin’s book&nbsp;
Fire And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.040
unfinished Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.920
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of&nbsp;
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:47.200
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold that&nbsp;
iconic seat, all the way up to the civil war that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.200
nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.080
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume&nbsp;
2 will continue from where part 1 ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:02.000
with Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's&nbsp;
reign and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.600
with Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and&nbsp;
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.960
The key event of the show is also the&nbsp;
key in the history of House Targaryen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.795
the Dance of the Dragons - the Targaryen civil&nbsp;
war, which divided the entire kingdom and launched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.795 --> 00:01:16.080
a huge war that was fought from 129 AC to 131 AC.
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.560
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.
A war of succession between Aegon II&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.720
and his half-sister Rhaenyra over&nbsp;
their father Viserys I's throne.
&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.800
Both of them thought they belonged on the&nbsp;
Iron Throne. When people started declaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.120
for one of them or the other, their&nbsp;
fight divided the kingdoms in two.
&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.160
Targaryens fought Targaryens, bothers&nbsp;
fought brothers, dragons fought dragons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.320
By the time it was over, thousands were dead.
One of the key characters in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.440
Targaryen civil war is Queen Alicent.
Alicent Hightower was a member of House Hightower
&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.120
who became the second wife&nbsp;
to King Viserys I Targaryen
&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.160
and therefore a Queen of the Targaryen dynasty.
She was the daughter of Ser Otto Hightower,
&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:02.480
who had been the Hand of the King to Jaehaerys&nbsp;
I, Viserys I, and later his grandson Aegon II.
&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:08.240
She was the mother of King Aegon II, Queen&nbsp;
Helaena, Prince Aemond and Prince Daeron.
&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.560
Alicent Hightower was in many ways&nbsp;
the true leader of Aegon II's faction
&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.440
during the Dance of the Dragons.
Alicent's father Otto Hightower had been Hand of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:24.240
the King in the last few years of the long reign&nbsp;
of King Jaehaerys I Targaryen. In 101 AC Otto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:29.360
brought the young Alicent to the royal court,
where she cared for the aging king.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.400
Jaehaerys eventually died in 103 AC,
while Alicent was reading to him and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.680
succeeded by his grandson Viserys I. 
Alicent stayed at court, as her father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.800
continued to occupy the position as the Hand
under Jaehaerys's grandson and successor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.680
King Viserys I Targaryen.
Already early in the reign of Viserys, Ser Otto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.560
and Prince Daemon Targaryen were at odds with each&nbsp;
other, and the court fool Mushroom has suggested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.280
that the quarrel between the two men began
when Daemon deflowered Alicent. The truths of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.080
these tales have never been uncovered.
Viserys I's first queen, Aemma Arryn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.600
only produced one living child&nbsp;
before her death - a daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.040
Rhaenyra. In the years that followed, Alicent&nbsp;
caught the eye of King Viserys I Targaryen,
&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.240
and Viserys chose Alicent as his&nbsp;
second wife. They married in 106 AC,
&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.640
despite the whispers of people who believed&nbsp;
that the Hand had risen above himself.
&nbsp;

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.440
Some doubted Alicent's virtue as rumors began&nbsp;
circling that she had given her maidenhead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:33.440
to Prince Daemon and had later even slept with&nbsp;
King Viserys while Queen Aemma was still alive.
&nbsp;

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:39.200
The notorious Mushroom suggested that Alicent had&nbsp;
been intimate with the late Jaehaerys as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:45.120
Nonetheless, Alicent was wed to Viserys. At&nbsp;
first young Rhaenyra and Alicent got along well,
&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.560
but a rift grew between them as soon as Alicent&nbsp;
produced her own children for Viserys I,
&nbsp;

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.440
and clearly wanted them to succeed&nbsp;
to the throne instead of her.
&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.120
Alicent bore Viserys I four&nbsp;
children: Aegon II, Aemond One-Eye,
&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.680
Daeron the Daring and Helaena (who&nbsp;
became the sister-wife of Aegon II).
&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.000
Over the years of Viserys I's reign, despite&nbsp;
his best efforts, a bitter rivalry grew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:15.920
between Alicent and Rhaenyra at court as well as&nbsp;
between their rival factions of supporters.
&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.520
In 111 AC, a great tourney&nbsp;
was held at King's Landing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:24.080
on the fifth anniversary of the King’s marriage&nbsp;
to Queen Alicent. At the opening feast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.960
Alicent wore a green gown while Princess&nbsp;
Rhaenyra dressed in Targaryen red and black.
&nbsp;

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:35.280
Soon afterward, their respective followers started&nbsp;
dressing in similar colors and styles to display&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:41.120
their political allegiance: Rhaenyra's faction&nbsp;
(the "Princess's followers") wore black clothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:44.480
and Alicent's faction ("the Queen's&nbsp;
followers") wore green clothing.
&nbsp;

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.680
Ultimately this inspired the nicknames for the&nbsp;
two factions: "the Blacks and the Greens".
&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.680
The Blacks (Rhaenyra's supporters) included&nbsp;
the Starks, Tullys, Arryns, Tarlys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.960
and Velaryons (among others), while the Greens&nbsp;
(Alicent's supporters) included the Hightowers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:05.120
and the Lannisters, among others. The Baratheons&nbsp;
started out as Blacks, but switched to the Greens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.920
when the civil war began, while the Tyrells&nbsp;
may have been Greens at first, but during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:15.440
civil war itself declared themselves neutral.
When Rhaenyra turned sixteen, the small council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:20.640
started looking for a suitable husband.
Alicent had her own choice: her eldest son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.880
Prince Aegon, who, while the princess was sixteen&nbsp;
years old, was only six years old himself. Viserys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:32.160
argued that the siblings had never gotten along,
but Alicent urged her husband that was all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.000
the more reason to wed the two.
Viserys refused, believing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.520
Alicent only made the suggestion to&nbsp;
get her own blood on the throne.
&nbsp;

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:46.480
Alicent's eldest son Aegon grew to be a lazy man,&nbsp;
prone to indulging his lusts with mistresses
&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:52.160
as well as prone to outbursts of anger. Given&nbsp;
that Aegon II had no great political skill,
&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:56.000
it was his mother Alicent who was seen&nbsp;
as the true leader of his faction
&nbsp;

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.480
however he was not necessarily an outright&nbsp;
puppet, as they shared the same goals.
&nbsp;

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.160
Alicent is the real political&nbsp;
mastermind behind her son.
&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.560
The Dance of the Dragons was seen so much&nbsp;
as a rivalry between Princess Rhaenyra and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.720
Queen Alicent that George R.R. Martin's&nbsp;
prequel novella about the conflict was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.600
titled "The Princess and the Queen", referring&nbsp;
to the two of them instead of to Aegon II.
&nbsp;

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.560
Viserys I publicly and repeatedly made&nbsp;
the great lords of the realm swear oaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.640
that Rhaenyra would succeed him on the&nbsp;
Iron Throne as the first Ruling Queen.
&nbsp;

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:32.800
A matter of hours after Viserys I died in&nbsp;
his sleep, however, Alicent staged a coup –
&nbsp;

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.760
one that she had been long&nbsp;
planning to the fine details. 
&nbsp;

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.840
One night, a servant found the old king had died&nbsp;
in his sleep and ran to inform Queen Alicent.
&nbsp;

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.160
Protocol dictated that the bells would&nbsp;
be rung, everyone notified and a raven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.320
sent to Dragonstone to summon the heir,&nbsp;
Princess Rhaenyra, for her coronation.
&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.640
But Alicent had other plans.
Once she saw her dead husband's body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:59.200
she sealed the room and had the servant thrown&nbsp;
into the Black Cells to ensure his silence.
&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:03.200
According to Mushroom, who was away&nbsp;
with Rhaenyra Targaryen on Dragonstone,
&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.160
Alicent poisoned Viserys's drink. True&nbsp;
or not, instead of announcing Viserys I's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.640
death immediately, Alicent warned Ser Criston&nbsp;
Cole, now Lord Commander of the Kingsguard,
&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.040
and together they called the small&nbsp;
council to discuss the succession,
&nbsp;

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.560
where plans were made to crown&nbsp;
Alicent's son Prince Aegon,
&nbsp;

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.400
instead of Princess Rhaenyra,&nbsp;
who had been Viserys's heir. 
&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.600
Of the seven-man council&nbsp;
(including her father Otto),
&nbsp;

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:33.120
all were Greens except for old&nbsp;
Master of Coin Lyman Beesbury. 
&nbsp;

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.360
Alicent soon made it clear that&nbsp;
she intended to crown Aegon II,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:42.000
against her late husband's wishes. 
The debate did not end till dawn when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.120
the Master of Coin declared this to be treason.
In response, Lord Commander of the Kingsguard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.640
Criston Cole silently snuck&nbsp;
behind Beesbury's chair,
&nbsp;

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:56.000
and without a word slashed his throat. As&nbsp;
the old man bled out onto the council table,
&nbsp;

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.400
the remaining council members seated&nbsp;
around it (including Alicent) continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:05.840
to plan out the next steps in their coup.
Her son rejected the Iron Throne at first, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.480
was told by Alicent that Rhaenyra would kill him&nbsp;
and his siblings if she was to become a Queen.
&nbsp;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:16.400
The coronation ceremony was soon after held&nbsp;
for Aegon II and Helaena, Aegon's sister-wife,
&nbsp;

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:20.080
in the Dragonpit while Rhaenyra&nbsp;
was crowned at Dragonstone.
&nbsp;

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.040
This rivalry exploded into&nbsp;
massive civil war between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:27.840
their two rival factions of House Targaryen,
a conflict known as the Dance of the Dragons.
&nbsp;

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:33.200
After the coronation, Alicent moved her chambers&nbsp;
to the Tower of the Hand, where her father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:39.120
resided. Every evening before bed, Queen Helaena&nbsp;
brought her children to see their grandmother.
&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.800
Because the Tower of the Hand was&nbsp;
less secure than Maegor's Holdfast,
&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:47.040
Blood and Cheese hired by Daemon were&nbsp;
able to take advantage of this custom.
&nbsp;

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:52.320
They sneaked into Alicent's chambers, slew&nbsp;
her bedmaid, and bound and gagged Alicent.
&nbsp;

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:58.000
When Helaena arrived with the children, they slew&nbsp;
Prince Jaehaerys, Aegon's eldest son and heir,
&nbsp;

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.120
as revenge for the death&nbsp;
of Rhaenyra's son Lucerys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:06.640
Helaena subsequently went mad with grief.
Aegon gave his surviving son, Prince Maelor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:11.520
to his mother Alicent to raise.
Later in the war, Aemond Targaryen foolishly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:16.800
led the Green army defending King's Landing north
to strike against Harrenhal, leaving the capital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.320
with only a skeleton defense.
Rhaenyra's forces were then able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:26.800
to take King's Landing in a surprise assault,
with Rhaenyra herself leading from dragon-back.
&nbsp;

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:32.000
The City Watch supported Rhaenyra as they were&nbsp;
loyal to Daemon and threw the gates open to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:38.080
her army, and also killed a few Green officers&nbsp;
that Aegon II had installed to command them,
&nbsp;

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:43.440
including Alicent's own brother Gwayne. Aegon&nbsp;
II was sneaked out of the city in secret.
&nbsp;

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:49.360
Several members of the Green Council, however,&nbsp;
were captured and executed as traitors - among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:55.360
them Alicent's father Otto. Alicent was also&nbsp;
captured, and Rhaenyra came to meet her.
&nbsp;

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.840
Despite the bitter rivalry between the two,&nbsp;
Rhaenyra announced that for the memory of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:05.200
the love of her father, she would spare Alicent's&nbsp;
life. During the exchange between the two queens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.520
Alicent made references to an old&nbsp;
rumor stating that Rhaenyra's first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.800
three sons were not legitimate Targaryens,
but the bastards from Ser Harwin Strong.
&nbsp;

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.880
According to Septon Eustace and Grand Maester&nbsp;
Munkun, Rhaenyra, furious at this accusation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.840
threatens Alicent to have her tongue removed&nbsp;
if she continued to spread this lie again.
&nbsp;

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:31.200
According to Mushroom, Rhaenyra's mistress of&nbsp;
whisperers and Daemon's former lover, Mysaria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:37.040
dissuaded her from taking Alicent's tongue and&nbsp;
instead suggested another terrible punishment,
&nbsp;

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:42.480
but also more poetic: Alicent and her&nbsp;
daughter should be sent to the Street of Silk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:47.280
to work as ladies of night. Mysaria&nbsp;
reportedly told Rhaenyra: ''Let them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:52.080
remain there until they are with child.
They speak of bastards so freely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:56.720
let them each have one of their own.''
Moreover, Mushroom cited this event as the cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:02.160
of Alicent's daughter's decision to end it all
as she probably got pregnant. Rhaenyra remained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:07.360
in control of the capital for about half a year,
but through several surprising turns of events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.240
Rhaenyra had to withdraw from the city and&nbsp;
the Greens recaptured it. As the armies of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:17.600
the Lads and Lord Cregan Stark advanced on the&nbsp;
capital, plotters plotted against Aegon II.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:21.680
The king was found poisoned and&nbsp;
Alicent was arrested by Velaryons.
&nbsp;

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:27.040
Aegon II had captured and fed Rhaenyra&nbsp;
to his dragon before his own death.
&nbsp;

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:32.880
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son took the throne&nbsp;
as Aegon III Targaryen in 131 AC. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:38.560
the Hour of the Wolf, Lord Cregan Stark punished&nbsp;
all men who betrayed King Aegon II and Alicent.
&nbsp;

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:43.680
While Cregan was Rhaenyra's supporter and had&nbsp;
believed that Aegon II had been a usurper
&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:49.040
and had been riding south to oust him from power,&nbsp;
Lord Stark did not believe in killing him,
&nbsp;

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:51.680
but rather in defeating him&nbsp;
on the field of battle. 
&nbsp;

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:56.480
Alicent survived through the end of the&nbsp;
war, but at great cost: all four of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:02.000
children and grandchildren had died. Therefore&nbsp;
Alicent lived to see her own bloodline end. 
&nbsp;

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:07.680
Alicent remained in her chambers for the&nbsp;
last year of her life. Alicent often wept,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:13.920
began talking to herself, and came to&nbsp;
dislike the color green. She died in 133 AC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:18.400
during the outbreak of Winter Fever.
Twenty major battles on land, in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:24.800
sky and on the sea, even more smaller battles,
and even more betrayals, turncloaks, and twists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:29.840
all of that and more this Game of Thrones prequel&nbsp;
show, House of the Dragon, brings in 2022.
&nbsp;

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:33.440
Let me know your thoughts about all of&nbsp;
this in the comment section down below.
&nbsp;

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.560
Thank you so much for watching and&nbsp;
I hope to see you in the next one.
&nbsp;

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.840
Peace!

